WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.792 --> 00:00:16.015
At home at Gloucester Castle, Edmund moved ahead with his plan to win his father's inheritance.

2
00:00:17.256 --> 00:00:21.938
He had forged a letter, and when he saw his father approaching, he made a great show of

3
00:00:22.058 --> 00:00:23.579
quickly putting it in his pocket.

4
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.280
"What are you hiding?"

5
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.821
asked the Earl of Gloucester.

6
00:00:26.841 --> 00:00:29.522
"It's nothing," replied his son.

7
00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:32.344
"Well, if it's nothing, why hide it?"

8
00:00:33.436 --> 00:00:34.896
Edmund pretended to be upset.

9
00:00:34.916 --> 00:00:37.297
"My lord, it's a letter from my brother.

10
00:00:37.857 --> 00:00:39.058
But I didn't want you to see it."

11
00:00:40.278 --> 00:00:41.878
"Give it to me," the earl ordered.

12
00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:44.099
He took the paper and began to read.

13
00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:45.680
"What's this?

14
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.381
Edgar doesn't want to wait until I die to inherit my estate and title!"

15
00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:51.721
sputtered Gloucester.

16
00:00:52.882 --> 00:00:56.963
"He wants me dead now, and then he will share his inheritance with you!

17
00:00:57.503 --> 00:00:58.263
Does he mean this?"

18
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:01.384
"Sir, I hope not," said Edmund.

19
00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.469
"I'll speak with him to find out more."

20
00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.152
"How can he be such a monster when I love him so dearly?"

21
00:01:08.693 --> 00:01:10.554
Outraged, Gloucester strode away.

22
00:01:11.815 --> 00:01:13.336
Soon after, Edgar appeared.

23
00:01:13.356 --> 00:01:15.117
"Good day, brother," he said.

24
00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:18.059
"What have you done to upset our father?"

25
00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:19.180
asked Edmund.

26
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.041
"I've done nothing!"

27
00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.642
Edgar replied, puzzled.

28
00:01:22.662 --> 00:01:27.245
"Well, he's so angry at you that I fear for your life!"

29
00:01:27.785 --> 00:01:28.506
Edmund exclaimed.

30
00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:31.568
"For now, you should avoid him.

31
00:01:32.044 --> 00:01:35.146
Go hide in my room, and carry a knife for safety."

32
00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:41.971
Edmund then promised to calm their father and arrange a meeting between the earl and Edgar that night.

33
00:01:42.431 --> 00:01:44.793
"I am on your side, brother," he lied.

34
00:01:45.914 --> 00:01:49.376
Meanwhile, Lear had settled into Goneril and Albany's castle.

35
00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:53.499
But Goneril had no patience for the old man and his knights.

36
00:01:53.519 --> 00:01:58.582
"They do nothing but cause trouble," she told her steward, Oswald.

37
00:01:58.602 --> 00:02:02.777
"When he returns from hunting, I don't want to see him.

38
00:02:03.898 --> 00:02:04.819
Tell him I'm sick.

39
00:02:05.359 --> 00:02:07.741
And I give you permission to ignore his demands.

40
00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:12.486
Tell the servants they don't have to always obey my father and his knights.

41
00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.748
If he doesn't like it, let him go to my sister's."

42
00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:21.453
When Lear returned, a man was waiting for him in the great hall of Goneril's castle.

43
00:02:21.954 --> 00:02:23.475
It was the loyal Earl of Kent.

44
00:02:24.656 --> 00:02:30.681
Rather than abandon his master, he had disguised himself as an ordinary servant so he could stay close

45
00:02:30.781 --> 00:02:31.742
and protect the king.

46
00:02:33.003 --> 00:02:35.725
Lear did not recognize him and asked, "Who are you?

47
00:02:36.265 --> 00:02:36.885
What do you want?"

48
00:02:36.905 --> 00:02:38.927
"I'm Caius.

49
00:02:39.507 --> 00:02:43.910
I'm honest, hardworking, and I want to serve you," replied Kent, bowing.

50
00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.033
"You seem to be a good fellow," said Lear.

51
00:02:47.053 --> 00:02:48.154
"Join my men."

52
00:02:49.294 --> 00:02:51.076
At that moment, Oswald appeared.

53
00:02:51.096 --> 00:02:53.277
"Where is my daughter?"

54
00:02:53.637 --> 00:02:54.138
asked Lear.

55
00:02:54.638 --> 00:02:56.920
But Oswald rudely left without replying.

56
00:02:57.404 --> 00:02:59.706
Lear was furious at this lack of respect.

57
00:03:00.807 --> 00:03:03.449
When Goneril finally entered the hall, she was frowning.

58
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.553
"Father! You must get rid of half your knights.

59
00:03:08.093 --> 00:03:11.256
They drink and fight and make too much noise," she complained.

60
00:03:11.276 --> 00:03:16.741
"Oh, how sharper than a serpent's tooth it is to have a thankless child!"

61
00:03:17.201 --> 00:03:17.801
snapped Lear.

62
00:03:17.821 --> 00:03:21.485
"It is your servants who are rude and unhelpful!

63
00:03:21.985 --> 00:03:25.328
How can you treat me like this, after all I've done for you?"

64
00:03:26.496 --> 00:03:28.378
He turned to Kent and his knights.

65
00:03:28.398 --> 00:03:30.339
"Prepare to go to Regan's.

66
00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.361
Surely she'll be kinder!"

67
00:03:33.502 --> 00:03:39.487
Before Lear's knights even began to saddle their horses, Goneril sent a letter to Regan, warning her that

68
00:03:39.527 --> 00:03:42.429
Lear was being difficult and was headed to her castle.

69
00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.092
Regan decided to leave rather than deal with her father.

70
00:03:47.173 --> 00:03:49.955
So she and Cornwall went to visit the Earl of Gloucester.

71
00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:54.719
When Lear arrived at Regan's, he could not believe she had left.

72
00:03:55.259 --> 00:03:56.792
"Come, then," he ordered his men.

73
00:03:56.812 --> 00:03:58.053
"To Gloucester's!"

74
00:03:59.313 --> 00:04:06.295
At Gloucester Castle, Edmund met Edgar in the courtyard and pulled him aside, saying quietly, "Our father's servants

75
00:04:06.415 --> 00:04:08.035
know you're hiding in my room.

76
00:04:09.236 --> 00:04:11.716
It's best you leave now, under cover of night."

77
00:04:12.216 --> 00:04:15.117
Just then they saw their father entering the courtyard.

78
00:04:15.137 --> 00:04:21.719
"Forgive me," whispered Edmund, "but I must draw my sword so our father doesn't suspect I want to

79
00:04:21.759 --> 00:04:22.139
help you.

80
00:04:23.279 --> 00:04:25.780
Now take your knife and pretend to defend yourself."

81
00:04:27.028 --> 00:04:31.630
When Edmund saw their father and his servants approaching, he shouted at Edgar, "Yield!

82
00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.651
Explain yourself to our father!"

83
00:04:34.851 --> 00:04:37.672
Then, whispering again, he told Edgar to flee.

84
00:04:38.253 --> 00:04:42.254
After Edgar ran away, Edmund cut his own arm with his sword.

85
00:04:43.495 --> 00:04:45.836
"Edmund, where is your villainous brother?"

86
00:04:46.296 --> 00:04:46.956
cried Gloucester.

87
00:04:46.976 --> 00:04:49.157
"He's gone, Father.

88
00:04:49.637 --> 00:04:51.118
He wanted me to murder you!

89
00:04:51.598 --> 00:04:54.459
When I refused, he attacked me and then fled.

90
00:04:54.959 --> 00:04:56.520
Look, he has wounded me!"

91
00:04:57.792 --> 00:04:59.434
Gloucester went pale with shock.

92
00:04:59.454 --> 00:05:04.318
"I will ask Cornwall to order that Edgar be hunted down and put to death!

93
00:05:05.018 --> 00:05:06.319
You are my only son now."

94
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:11.304
"My plan is working perfectly," thought Edmund with great glee.

95
00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:13.966
Just then trumpets sounded.

96
00:05:14.566 --> 00:05:19.350
Regan and Cornwall entered the courtyard, and Gloucester told them of Edgar's evil deeds.

97
00:05:19.891 --> 00:05:21.973
They praised Edmund for being so loyal.

98
00:05:23.174 --> 00:05:25.576
Finally, Gloucester asked, "Why have you come?"

99
00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.741
"It's about my father.

100
00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:31.242
We need your advice," said Regan, flattering the earl.

101
00:05:32.382 --> 00:05:34.283
Gloucester bowed and led them inside.

102
00:05:35.464 --> 00:05:41.106
A few hours later, Lear arrived at Gloucester castle and asked to see his daughter and Cornwall.

103
00:05:41.126 --> 00:05:46.769
"I'm sorry," Gloucester told him, "they say they are tired and cannot see you."

104
00:05:47.869 --> 00:05:50.630
"They refuse to see me simply because they are tired?"

105
00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:51.671
shouted Lear.

106
00:05:51.691 --> 00:05:54.792
"Tell my daughter I command her to speak with me!"

107
00:05:55.948 --> 00:05:59.349
Gloucester left and soon returned with Regan and Cornwall.

108
00:05:59.369 --> 00:06:03.611
"Father, I am glad to see you," murmured Regan.

109
00:06:03.631 --> 00:06:07.733
"I should hope so," said Lear, "for are you not my daughter?

110
00:06:08.953 --> 00:06:13.035
Oh, beloved Regan, your sister Goneril has treated me shamefully!"

111
00:06:13.055 --> 00:06:18.557
"Father, you are judging Goneril too harshly," Regan replied coolly.

112
00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:21.999
"I'm sure my sister is being more than fair.

113
00:06:22.499 --> 00:06:25.280
Return to Goneril and ask for forgiveness."

114
00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:27.501
"Forgiveness for what?

115
00:06:28.061 --> 00:06:32.385
She wants to take away half my knights, and she's wounded my heart with her cruel words.

116
00:06:32.966 --> 00:06:34.026
Curses on your sister!"

117
00:06:34.046 --> 00:06:37.850
"Calm yourself, sir," chided Cornwall.

118
00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.594
"Father," Regan said, "your age is making you foolish.

119
00:06:42.954 --> 00:06:44.435
You must take my advice."

120
00:06:44.455 --> 00:06:47.238
"I will never return to your sister!"

121
00:06:47.698 --> 00:06:48.258
bellowed Lear.

122
00:06:48.779 --> 00:06:51.401
"Regan, surely, you are grateful for what I've done for you."

123
00:06:52.622 --> 00:06:54.624
Suddenly, the trumpets sounded again.

124
00:06:55.188 --> 00:06:56.789
In the doorway stood Goneril!

125
00:06:56.809 --> 00:07:01.712
"Goneril," said Lear, stunned, "are you not ashamed to look at me?"

126
00:07:02.852 --> 00:07:03.633
"Why should I be?"

127
00:07:04.153 --> 00:07:05.254
asked Goneril coldly.

128
00:07:05.274 --> 00:07:06.634
"What have I done wrong?"

129
00:07:07.155 --> 00:07:09.116
She walked over to Regan, who took her hand.

130
00:07:09.136 --> 00:07:14.419
"Father, I am not ready to care for you and all your men," said Regan.

131
00:07:14.439 --> 00:07:19.922
"Goneril is right—having too many people in one castle causes problems.

132
00:07:20.482 --> 00:07:22.143
Why not keep just 50 knights?

133
00:07:22.623 --> 00:07:25.112
Or even 25?"

134
00:07:25.152 --> 00:07:26.012
"Or why keep any?"

135
00:07:26.432 --> 00:07:27.133
Goneril added.

136
00:07:27.153 --> 00:07:29.753
"Indeed," said Regan.

137
00:07:29.773 --> 00:07:32.074
"Our own servants can look after you."

138
00:07:33.214 --> 00:07:35.315
Lear was wounded by his daughters' coldness.

139
00:07:35.335 --> 00:07:37.415
"Both of you have turned against me!"

140
00:07:37.736 --> 00:07:38.156
he cried.

141
00:07:39.296 --> 00:07:41.657
How small Cordelia's fault seems now.

142
00:07:42.297 --> 00:07:43.957
Oh, I must not weep!

143
00:07:44.637 --> 00:07:46.758
Instead, I shall take my revenge—!"

144
00:07:48.078 --> 00:07:51.919
A thunderclap drowned out his words as he strode through the castle gates.

145
00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.940
Rain began to pelt down.

146
00:07:55.156 --> 00:07:59.537
"I don't know where he's going," said Gloucester, worried, "and there's no shelter close by."

147
00:07:59.557 --> 00:08:02.898
"It's his own fault," said Goneril.

148
00:08:02.918 --> 00:08:06.699
"And this will teach him a lesson," added Regan.

149
00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:08.620
"Regan is right.

150
00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.281
Lock your castle doors," barked Cornwall.

151
00:08:12.461 --> 00:08:14.682
A huge bolt of lightning lit up the sky.

152
00:08:15.162 --> 00:08:17.062
The storm was gathering force.
